# .github/.releaseignore -- dev-only paths for the release gate (gitignore syntax).
# A merged PR whose changed files ALL match here releases nothing, unless it carries a
# semver:* label (an explicit label always wins). Anything not matched is product and
# releases as a patch. Read by .github/workflows/release.yml.
# NOTE git semantics: a file can't be re-included if a parent DIRECTORY is excluded.
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/**   does NOT work (docs/user/ itself is excluded);
#   docs/**  +  !docs/user/  +  !docs/user/**   does. File-level `!docs/openapi.yaml` works.
#
# Product (deliberately NOT listed): everything the Dockerfile COPYs (go.mod/go.sum, cmd/,
# internal/ incl. embedded assets + templates, docs/openapi.go + docs/openapi.yaml), deploy/
# (Helm chart), README.md, compose.yaml, .dockerignore, and the Claude plugin
# (plugins/, .claude-plugin/), which is published to users. Wiki content (the vault) is not
# in this repo.

# CI and dev environment
/.github/
/.devcontainer/
/.claude/
/.mcp.json
/.golangci*
/.pre-commit-config.yaml
/.editorconfig
/.gitignore
/.markdownlint*
/.yamllint*

# Agent and contributor docs
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
/CONTRIBUTING*

# Developer docs only: docs/*.md is never COPYed into the image or served.
# docs/openapi.go and docs/openapi.yaml are embedded and served, so they stay product.
/docs/*.md

# Dev tooling not used by the Dockerfile or chart
/scripts/

# Tests and fixtures
*_test.go
testdata/
